IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pcol-rules`

-- Protection of Cultural Objects on Loan Act 2013 (Cth) — the encoder's tests.

§ `Tests`

`foreign museum` MEANS `a corporation incorporated under a foreign law`
`ordinary` MEANS `an ordinary statutory power`

GIVEN asked IS A DATE, prc IS A `Proceeding`, pw IS A `Power`
GIVETH A `Loan case`
`a loan asked on` asked `facing` prc `under` pw MEANS
    `Loan case` OF `foreign museum`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE,
                   Date 15 3 2026, NOTHING, NOTHING, asked, prc, pw

-- s 8(1)
#ASSERT `Part 2 applies` (`a loan asked on` (Date 1 4 2026) `facing` `none` `under` `ordinary`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Part 2 applies` (`Loan case` OF `another person`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, Date 15 3 2026, NOTHING, NOTHING, Date 1 4 2026, `none`, `ordinary`))
#ASSERT NOT (`Part 2 applies` (`Loan case` OF `foreign museum`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, Date 15 3 2026, NOTHING, NOTHING, Date 1 4 2026, `none`, `ordinary`))
#ASSERT NOT (`Part 2 applies` (`Loan case` OF `foreign museum`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, Date 15 3 2026, NOTHING, NOTHING, Date 1 4 2026, `none`, `ordinary`))
-- s 8(2): imported 15 March 2026, protected to 14 March 2028.
#ASSERT `protection ends for` (`a loan asked on` (Date 1 4 2026) `facing` `none` `under` `ordinary`) EQUALS JUST (Date 14 3 2028)
#ASSERT `it is protected then` (`a loan asked on` (Date 14 3 2028) `facing` `none` `under` `ordinary`)
#ASSERT NOT (`it is protected then` (`a loan asked on` (Date 15 3 2028) `facing` `none` `under` `ordinary`))
-- export earlier; a later ministerial day
#ASSERT `protection ends for` (`Loan case` OF `foreign museum`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, Date 15 3 2026, JUST (Date 1 9 2026), NOTHING, Date 1 4 2026, `none`, `ordinary`) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2026)
#ASSERT `protection ends for` (`Loan case` OF `foreign museum`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, Date 15 3 2026, NOTHING, JUST (Date 30 6 2028), Date 1 4 2026, `none`, `ordinary`) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 6 2028)
-- 29 February 2028 import: ends 28 February 2030
#ASSERT `protection ends for` (`Loan case` OF `foreign museum`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, Date 29 2 2028, NOTHING, NOTHING, Date 1 4 2028, `none`, `ordinary`) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2030)
-- ss 9-10
#ASSERT `the proceeding is barred` (`a loan asked on` (Date 1 4 2026) `facing` `a claim against the object itself` `under` `ordinary`)
#ASSERT `the proceeding is barred` (`a loan asked on` (Date 1 4 2026) `facing` `a claim against me personally about the object` `under` `ordinary`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the proceeding is barred` (`a loan asked on` (Date 1 4 2026) `facing` `proceedings under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 or prescribed` `under` `ordinary`))
-- ss 11-12
#ASSERT NOT (`it can be seized` (`a loan asked on` (Date 1 4 2026) `facing` `none` `under` `ordinary`))
#ASSERT `it can be seized` (`a loan asked on` (Date 1 4 2026) `facing` `none` `under` `a seizure power given only to police`)
#ASSERT NOT (`it can be forfeited` (`a loan asked on` (Date 1 4 2026) `facing` `none` `under` `a seizure power given only to police`))
#ASSERT `it can be forfeited` (`a loan asked on` (Date 1 4 2026) `facing` `none` `under` `Part IAA of the Crimes Act 1914`)
#ASSERT `it can be seized` (`a loan asked on` (Date 1 4 2029) `facing` `none` `under` `ordinary`)
